+- **`lib/proposal-payment-schedule.ts` (new)** — the pure, self-balancing resolver. seq-0 = the downpayment = the guest-side LOCK amount; an auto "Final balance" row is the exact integer remainder so the RAW plan always pays to ₱0 against the quote total (line items + crew/transport − discount). Installments are fixed ₱ or % of total. The crew-meal "offset — couple provides" CREDIT is deducted from the FINAL installment first, cascading upward (reuses `applyCreditToFinalInstallment` from `lib/package-line-pricing.ts`) — the downpayment is never eaten; a credit that exceeds everything-but-the-downpayment leaves the lock whole and flags `credit_over` ("trim a payment"). Pure + total (never throws); `sanitizeAndResolveSchedule` re-resolves server-side so persisted numbers are authoritative, never the client's arithmetic. Backed by `lib/proposal-payment-schedule.test.ts` (10 cases pinning the ₱0 guarantee, downpayment protection, %/fixed mixes, over/credit-over edges, add-payment idempotence).
+- **`app/_components/proposal-maker.tsx`** — replaced the % downpayment PREVIEW with a real schedule editor (installment rows, gold "locks" tag on seq-0, ₱/% toggle, due timing On booking / N days before / Event day, auto "Final balance" row, "Add payment · splits the balance", live "balances to ₱0" / "over — trim a payment"). Replaced the cosmetic method chips with a real picker over the vendor's published `vendor_payment_methods` (default-selects approved+shown; untick-all = show all approved). Both ride the existing `payload` → `sendCustomProposalFromChat`.
+- **`lib/proposal-send.ts`** — `sendCustomProposalCore` re-resolves the schedule and validates the picked method ids against the vendor's OWN methods (RLS-scoped intersect; spoofed ids dropped), persisting both new columns at insert. Line-item send path + gate unchanged.
+- **`lib/vendor-payment-methods.server.ts`** — `fetchProposalPaymentMethods` (admin-read of the vendor's approved+shown methods for a proposal the RLS read already gated; links stay pro-tier-gated; QR presigned).
+- **`app/proposals/[publicId]/page.tsx`** — couple-facing render of the schedule (installments + due timing + "locks the date" badge + crew-credit annotation + plan total) and "How to pay" (BDO/GCash/Maya/bank details + QR). Older proposals with `{}` schedule / no methods degrade to line items only.
+- **`app/vendor-dashboard/messages/[threadId]/page.tsx`** — fetches the vendor's own payment methods (best-effort, in the existing parallel batch) and passes them to the editor.
+- **Migration `20270723118427_vendor_proposals_payment_schedule_methods.sql`** — additive, idempotent: `ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS payment_schedule jsonb DEFAULT '{}'` + `payment_method_ids jsonb DEFAULT '[]'` on `vendor_proposals`. RLS unchanged (columns set at the vendor's own draft insert). NOT yet applied to prod (owner will).
+
+Graceful-degrade + additive throughout: an existing proposal without a schedule still renders; the shipped line-item editor + send path are untouched.
+
+SPEC IMPACT: Vendor_Proposal_Maker_2026-07-10.md § 8 + § 9 (the deferred half; now implemented — the earlier "deferred" note in the PR-3/§ "Build plan" is superseded).
